<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's CVRD in $1 bln pulp venture.</title>
<headline>Brazil's CVRD in $1 bln pulp venture.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Cia. Vale do Rio Doce (CVRD) and Ripasa are teaming with Japan's Nissho Iwai Corp in a $1 billion joint venture to produce pulp in northeastern Brazilian state of Maranhao, officials said.</p>
<p>The formal announcement will be made at a news conference Wednesday in Rio de Janeiro at 1100 local/1400 GMT, said a statement from officials of Celmar Industria de Celulose e Papel, the new company resulting from the partnership.</p>
<p>Celmar will become Brazil's second-largest pulp maker, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
